glab-tui is a terminal user interface for GitLab and GitHub, built on top
of the glab and gh command line tools.  It detects the hosting service of
the current repository and translates every action into the matching CLI
command, so no separate API credentials are needed.

Issues, merge and pull requests, pipelines, runners, releases, todos and
milestones each get their own tab, with fuzzy search, bulk editing, inline
code review with syntax highlighted diffs, configurable keybindings and
themes.
